{%- comment -%}
  Section: Main product
  Phase 4, Stage 1 (media gallery + core info) + Stage 2 (native variant
  selection + a working product form) + Stage 3 (quantity selector) +
  Stage 4B (AJAX add-to-cart) + Stage 5 (sold-out/unavailable states) +
  Stage 6 (Details/Delivery/Returns accordions). Still no recommendations —
  a later Phase 4 stage layers that onto this same section.

  Stage 6: three merchant-editable blocks (details/delivery/returns),
  looped in whatever order the merchant has arranged them via section.
  blocks — templates/product.json pre-populates the default instance of
  all three, in that order, but this loop itself doesn't hardcode a count
  or order beyond what the merchant configures. Details always sources
  product.description rather than having its own rich-text setting (that's
  the point of the block — showing the real product's real description);
  Delivery/Returns are plain merchant-editable richtext. Any block whose
  resulting content is blank is skipped entirely (no empty accordion
  panel) — except Details in the Theme Editor specifically, where a
  placeholder string takes over so the block stays visible/selectable
  while merchants are looking at a product with no description yet.

  Stage 5: availability is driven entirely by variant.available/product.
  available (never inventory_quantity, which isn't exposed to the
  storefront and isn't guaranteed-live even if it were) — this
  automatically respects Shopify's own inventory policy, including
  continue-selling-when-out-of-stock variants, with no extra theme logic.
  has_valid_variant/is_purchasable below distinguish two different
  "can't buy this" cases with two different labels: current_variant is
  always some real, existing variant for any real Shopify product (product.
  selected_or_first_available_variant never actually returns blank, and an
  invalid ?variant= param is silently ignored by Shopify in favor of a
  normal fallback) — a real variant that's simply out of stock shows
  "Sold out". has_valid_variant only goes false in the deliberately
  defensive, practically unreachable case of a product resolving to no
  variant object at all, which shows "Unavailable" instead — a distinct
  label for "there is nothing here to select" versus "this specific
  option is out of stock."

  Stage 4B: assets/theme.js intercepts this form's submit only when JS runs
  (a real submit event listener via e.preventDefault(), not a rebuilt
  form) and POSTs its own FormData to cart/add.js with sections=cart-drawer
  bundled in, so the drawer refresh always comes from Liquid's own render
  of real cart state — nothing about the form's no-JS behavior changes.
  data-product-form-error is the dedicated inline error target for a 422/
  non-2xx response (kept empty/hidden server-side); data-label-added-to-
  cart carries the pre-translated "added to cart" prefix JS uses for its
  accessible success announcement, sourced from Liquid so nothing is
  hardcoded in JS.

  The quantity input is a plain name="quantity" number field (min="1",
  required) inside the same already-working form. Without JS, native HTML5
  constraint validation on those two attributes blocks submitting anything
  empty or below 1 — the browser stops the form and prompts a fix, rather
  than silently rewriting the value, since only JS can do that. With JS,
  assets/theme.js actively normalizes the field to a valid whole number on
  change (before the browser's own validation would ever run), and the +/-
  buttons (type="button", never touching submission) call the same
  normalization. Quantity defaults to 1 on load, matching every other
  Shopify PDP.

  The breadcrumb trail is real (Home / current collection / product title)
  rather than the prototype's static "Back to listing" link, using the
  global collection object when arriving from a collection page and falling
  back to the product's first collection otherwise.

  The form uses Shopify's native {% form 'product' %} tag's return_to
  param, which the tag turns into its own hidden <input name="return_to">
  automatically (adding a second one manually would duplicate that field
  in the POST body). return_to: 'back' was tried first, since routes.
  cart_url / templates/cart.json don't exist until Stage 4 and a plain
  non-JS submit must not land on a 404 there — but verified against the
  real /cart/add endpoint, the literal value "back" is not resolved
  against the request's Referer and instead falls through to the shop
  root, not this page. An explicit return_to value (a real path) is
  honored correctly, so request.path — the current PDP path including any
  ?variant= already in the address bar — is used instead to actually
  satisfy "return to the PDP".

  Variant data for the Stage 2 JS enhancement (assets/theme.js, the
  data-variant-radio change handler) is embedded once below as JSON, with
  every price already run through Liquid's money filter server-side — this
  keeps the client free of any currency-formatting logic of its own, so it
  never hardcodes EUR and stays correct for any shop currency/format.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign current_variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  assign has_valid_variant = false
  if current_variant != blank and current_variant.id != blank
    assign has_valid_variant = true
  endif

  assign is_purchasable = false
  if has_valid_variant and current_variant.available
    assign is_purchasable = true
  endif

  assign show_compare_at = false
  assign discount_percent = 0
  if has_valid_variant and current_variant.compare_at_price > current_variant.price
    assign show_compare_at = true
    assign discount_percent = current_variant.compare_at_price | minus: current_variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: current_variant.compare_at_price | round
  endif

  assign breadcrumb_collection = collection
  if breadcrumb_collection == blank and product.collections.first != blank
    assign breadcrumb_collection = product.collections.first
  endif

  assign product_form_id = 'ProductForm-' | append: section.id
  assign added_to_cart_label = 'cart.item_added' | t
-%}
{%- capture variants_json -%}
  [
    {%- for variant in product.variants -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign v_show_compare_at = false
        assign v_discount_percent = 0
        if variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
          assign v_show_compare_at = true
          assign v_discount_percent = variant.compare_at_price | minus: variant.price | times: 100.0 | divided_by: variant.compare_at_price | round
        endif
      -%}
      {
        "id": {{ variant.id | json }},
        "available": {{ variant.available | json }},
        "price": {{ variant.price | money | json }},
        "compareAtPrice": {% if v_show_compare_at %}{{ variant.compare_at_price | money | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %},
        "discountPercent": {{ v_discount_percent | json }},
        "sku": {{ variant.sku | json }},
        "featuredMediaId": {% if variant.featured_media %}{{ variant.featured_media.id | json }}{% else %}null{% endif %}
      }{% unless forloop.last %},{% endunless %}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
{%- endcapture -%}
<section class="product" {{ section.shopify_attributes }}>
  <nav class="product__breadcrumb" aria-label="{{ 'product.breadcrumb_label' | t }}">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ 'product.breadcrumb_home' | t }}</a>
    <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    {%- if breadcrumb_collection != blank -%}
      <a href="{{ breadcrumb_collection.url }}">{{ breadcrumb_collection.title }}</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="product__breadcrumb-current" aria-current="page">{{ product.title }}</span>
  </nav>

  <div class="product__layout">
    <div class="product__media">
      {%- render 'product-gallery', product: product -%}
    </div>

    <div class="product__info">
      <div class="product__title-row">
        <div>
          {%- if product.vendor != blank -%}
            <span class="product__vendor">{{ product.vendor }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
          <h1 class="product__title">{{ product.title }}</h1>
        </div>
        {%- render 'wishlist-button', product: product -%}
      </div>

      {%- form 'product', product, return_to: request.path, id: product_form_id, class: 'product__form', data-product-form: '', data-label-added-to-cart: added_to_cart_label -%}
        <div class="product-form-error" data-product-form-error data-label-generic-error="{{ 'cart.generic_error' | t }}" role="alert" aria-live="assertive" hidden></div>

        <div class="product__price-row">
          <span class="product__price" data-product-price>{% if has_valid_variant %}{{ current_variant.price | money }}{% else %}{{ 0 | money }}{% endif %}</span>
          <span class="product__compare-at" data-product-compare-at {% unless show_compare_at %}hidden{% endunless %}>{{ current_variant.compare_at_price | money }}</span>
          <span class="product__discount" data-product-discount {% unless show_compare_at %}hidden{% endunless %}>&minus;{{ discount_percent }}%</span>
        </div>

        {%- render 'product-variant-picker', product: product, current_variant: current_variant -%}

        <p
          class="product__availability{% unless is_purchasable %} product__availability--sold-out{% endunless %}"
          data-product-availability
          data-label-in-stock="{{ 'product.availability_in_stock' | t }}"
          data-label-sold-out="{{ 'product.availability_sold_out' | t }}"
        >
          {%- if is_purchasable -%}
            {{- 'product.availability_in_stock' | t -}}
          {%- elsif has_valid_variant -%}
            {{- 'product.availability_sold_out' | t -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- 'product.availability_unavailable' | t -}}
          {%- endif -%}
        </p>

        <p
          class="product__sku"
          data-product-sku
          data-label-sku-prefix="{{ 'product.sku_prefix' | t }}"
          {% if current_variant.sku == blank %}hidden{% endif %}
        >{{ 'product.sku_prefix' | t }}{{ current_variant.sku }}</p>

        <div class="product__quantity" data-product-quantity>
          <label class="product__quantity-label" for="Quantity-{{ product_form_id }}">{{ 'product.quantity_label' | t }}</label>
          <div class="product__quantity-controls">
            <button
              type="button"
              class="product__quantity-btn product__quantity-btn--minus"
              data-quantity-decrease
              aria-label="{{ 'product.quantity_decrease' | t }}"
            >
              {%- render 'icon', icon: 'minus', size: 14 -%}
            </button>
            <input
              type="number"
              name="quantity"
              id="Quantity-{{ product_form_id }}"
              class="product__quantity-input"
              min="1"
              step="1"
              inputmode="numeric"
              value="1"
              required
              data-quantity-input
            >
            <button
              type="button"
              class="product__quantity-btn product__quantity-btn--plus"
              data-quantity-increase
              aria-label="{{ 'product.quantity_increase' | t }}"
            >
              {%- render 'icon', icon: 'plus', size: 14 -%}
            </button>
          </div>
          <span class="visually-hidden" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-quantity-announcer data-label-quantity-prefix="{{ 'product.quantity_announce' | t }}"></span>
        </div>

        <button
          type="submit"
          name="add"
          class="product__submit"
          data-product-submit
          data-label-add="{{ 'product.add_to_cart' | t }}"
          data-label-sold-out="{{ 'product.sold_out' | t }}"
          data-label-unavailable="{{ 'product.unavailable' | t }}"
          {% unless is_purchasable %}disabled{% endunless %}
        >
          {%- if is_purchasable -%}
            {{- 'product.add_to_cart' | t -}}
          {%- elsif has_valid_variant -%}
            {{- 'product.sold_out' | t -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- 'product.unavailable' | t -}}
          {%- endif -%}
        </button>

        <script type="application/json" data-product-variants>{{ variants_json }}</script>
      {%- endform -%}

      <p class="product__reassurance">{{ 'product.reassurance' | t }}</p>

      {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
        <div class="product-accordion">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- case block.type -%}
              {%- when 'details' -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign details_content = product.description
                  if details_content == blank and request.design_mode
                    assign details_content = 'product.accordion_details_placeholder' | t
                  endif
                -%}
                {%- if details_content != blank -%}
                  {%- render 'product-accordion', heading: block.settings.heading, content: details_content, id: block.id, block: block -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- when 'delivery' or 'returns' -%}
                {%- if block.settings.content != blank -%}
                  {%- render 'product-accordion', heading: block.settings.heading, content: block.settings.content, id: block.id, block: block -%}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endcase -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Main product",
  "settings": [],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "details",
      "name": "Details",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Product details"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "delivery",
      "name": "Delivery",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Delivery"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "Content",
          "default": "<p>Orders are processed within 1–2 business days and ship from our warehouse. Delivery typically takes 2–4 business days once dispatched, and you'll get a shipping confirmation email with tracking as soon as it's on its way.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "returns",
      "name": "Returns",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "heading",
          "label": "Heading",
          "default": "Returns"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "content",
          "label": "Content",
          "default": "<p>Not the right fit? Items can be returned within 30 days of delivery, unworn and in their original packaging. Get in touch and we'll walk you through the next steps.</p>"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
